(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[7 1 "// str's methods (Objects/unicodeobject.c), str.format aside (PY5c's, format.go). Case mappings are"] [8 1 "// Go's simple ones (PY5b: CPython's full mappings, ß to SS, are a recorded difference)."] [46 43 "// the rest as it is, its trailing whitespace kept (PY6c)"] [71 43 "// the rest as it is, its leading whitespace kept (PY6c)"] [87 1 "// kwArgs splits a method's arguments: positional ones (self excluded) and keywords by name."] [155 18 "// a start beyond the end: an empty range past stop, so nothing matches, \"\" neither (ADJUST_INDICES; PY6c)"] [168 1 "// runeIndex finds sub in rs[start:stop] (from the end when last): its index, or -1. A one-code-point sub is"] [169 1 "// looked for directly; a longer one in windows that double from the end it searches from (256 code points"] [170 1 "// first), each window searched by runeIndexRange, so that a match's cost is its distance from that end, as"] [171 1 "// CPython's fastsearch's, not the whole range's (py-limits-1125: find(';', i) in a loop over a non-ASCII str"] [172 1 "// encoded rs[start:stop] whole at each call, quadratic: 40,000 calls on 320 KB took 25 s)."] [197 3 "// the matches that end in (hi-n, hi], the window's, are right of every one a later window holds"] [209 2 "// the matches that start in [lo, lo+n), the window's, are left of every one a later window holds"] [222 1 "// runeIndexRange is runeIndex's search of one range, rs[start:stop] encoded whole."] [227 2 "// the search by Go's strings.Index on a fixed-width encoding of the code points (one byte each when all are"] [228 2 "// below 0x100, else four, a match kept only at a code point's boundary): compiled, so the large searches of"] [229 2 "// string_tests' test_adaptive_find run in time on goi (PY6c)"] [323 19 "// one exact str: itself (PyUnicode_Join; PY6c)"] [361 14 "// from the right, also without maxsplit: 'abbbc'.rsplit('bb') is ['ab', 'c'] (PY6c)"] [435 4 "// PyUnicode_Substring's unicode_result_unchanged: an exact str with nothing stripped is itself (queue 328:"] [436 4 "// test_bigmem's test_lstrip)"] [443 33 "// the Unicode database's mappings (PY6c, unicodedata_str.go)"] [484 4 "// an ASCII str by its bytes (py-mods-1122: Runes copies an ASCII str whole, each call O(len), so a parser's"] [485 4 "// startswith(x, pos) in a loop was quadratic)"] [500 16 "// a code point past ASCII is in no ASCII str"] [563 6 "// an ASCII str by its bytes (py-mods-1122: Runes copied it whole each call, so find(x, start) in a loop"] [564 6 "// was quadratic: email's _parseparam, test_email's test_get_param_linear_complexity)"] [614 4 "// an ASCII str by its bytes (py-mods-1122: as find)"] [850 3 "// bytes.hex(sep=, bytes_per_sep=1): pystrhex.c's separators (strhex, the data family's binascii)"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[81 27] [81 34] [154 29] [181 21] [181 33] [188 17] [188 27] [198 17] [198 19] [203 49] [210 17] [210 19] [215 49] [256 22] [256 24] [267 14] [267 16] [281 46] [303 46] [312 48] [314 45] [322 34] [396 31] [427 47] [463 40] [479 32] [494 36] [516 35] [541 40] [591 42] [647 30] [655 40] [689 14] [689 24] [703 42] [723 47] [752 53] [762 53] [778 31] [789 16] [789 23] [858 30]]} (go/file "strmethods.go" :imports [


